Z||000002||rockcrawl||01-08-2001||05:03 PM||||There's a company called Baumann Engineering that makes a stand alone controller for the Ford electronic transmissions. If you could find something like that for the 4T80e, you'd be in business. <A HREF="http://www.baumannengineering.com/elect.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.baumannengineering.com/elect.htm</A> <P>Otherwise I'd say a 4T60 from a '91 4.9 Cadillac would be the best bet. They are built to handle at least 200hp, 275ft/lb. After '91 they were electronic. Not sure how much hp & tq the 3800s were putting out before '91, maybe the 3800 4T60 is just as good.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
